WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:06.700
What would happen if all the humans on Earth
disappeared tomorrow?

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:11.531
Well these real life ghost towns, which have
all been abandoned for various reasons, give

00:00:11.531 --> 00:00:22.360
a glimpse into what life would be like when
nature is left to reclaim man-made places.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:24.540
First up is Hashima Island.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:29.920
Commonly referred to as Battleship Island,
due to its resemblance to a Japanese battleship.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:34.390
On a side note, why do Japanese battleships
look so darn creepy!

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:40.460
This abandoned island is one of 505 uninhabited
islands off the south-west coast of Japan.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:45.440
What makes this island different from it's
504 other neighbouring islands is that Hashima

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:48.920
Island used to be a thriving mining community.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:54.649
In 1887, during the industrialisation of Japan
this island was setup as an undersea coal

00:00:54.649 --> 00:00:56.420
mining facility.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:01:00.720
Many of the miners lived on the island all
year round so the island functioned as an

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:06.770
offshore city, including living quarters and
all the conveniences of a regular city.

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:12.150
Thousands of people lived and worked on the
island during its 87 years of operation.

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:17.030
Hitting a peak population of 5,259 people
in 1959.

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:24.190
However, in 1974 the mine was closed down
and all the residents left the island.

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:29.810
Due to years of neglect and a lack of maintenance
the island is now in ruins.

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:34.900
Nature has reclaimed many of the building,
which are now highly unstable and many of

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:36.670
them have collapsed.

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:40.320
The whole island is like an eerie, post-apocalyptic
nightmare.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:44.220
Speckled with the faintest memories of miners
who spent their lives there.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:49.350
It has since become somewhat of a tourist
attraction in Japan but tourists should be

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:54.670
wary, as it's a dangerous place that has seen
no maintenance and the buildings could easily

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:57.280
crumble at any moment.

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:02.790
Ah Disney World, Florida - full of happiness
and smug little kids.

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:05.610
Surely nothing bad could happen here?

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:06.960
On the contrary!

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.260
You wouldn't think it, but Disney World Resort
in Orlando, Florida, is home to one of the

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:14.110
most bone-chilling, abandoned places on Earth.

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:19.480
In 1965 Walt Disney bought an island in the
middle of Bay Lake at the Orlando based Disney

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:20.670
World Resort.

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:26.739
He originally named it Treasure Island but
later changed it to Discovery Island, to stop

00:02:26.739 --> 00:02:28.790
people digging up the soil.

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:32.830
The island was officially opened to guests
in 1974.

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:37.580
Discovery Island was a wildlife attraction
where guests could observe rare species such

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:43.069
as Scarlet Ibises, Galapagos tortoises, lemurs
and many others.

00:02:43.069 --> 00:02:50.660
All was going well, until July 9th, 1999 when
the island was suddenly closed to the public

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:56.129
and all the animals were hastily relocated
to zoos away from the island.

00:02:56.129 --> 00:03:01.989
It isn't known why the Discovery Island attraction
was closed but many rumours have suggested

00:03:01.989 --> 00:03:08.160
that a bacterium capable of killing humans
called amoeba was discovered in the waters

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:09.880
surrounding the island.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:10.880
Oops!

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:16.099
The island was simply abandoned and was left
to be taken over by the wild.

00:03:16.099 --> 00:03:21.070
Very few have stepped foot on the island ever
since, and today it's an eerie reminder of

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:24.160
the fun park attraction that once was.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:29.739
The island is full of abandoned buildings
and attractions, all engulfed by nature.

00:03:29.739 --> 00:03:34.400
The island is now home to a family of highly
aggressive vultures as well as some other

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:39.600
bizarre items such as preserved snakes in
jars.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:45.130
This derelict and potentially life-threatening
island still sits, undisturbed and quietly

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:49.989
concealing its mysteries, right in the middle
of the bright lights and commercial perfection

00:03:49.989 --> 00:03:52.849
that is Disney World Florida.

00:03:52.849 --> 00:03:58.430
It was the early 21st century in Ireland and
the country was in the middle of a housing

00:03:58.430 --> 00:03:59.430
bubble.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:04.370
Houses were selling like hot cakes and property
development was happening at an unprecedented

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:05.370
rate.

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:11.730
But then the luck of the Irish ran out and
in 2008 the housing market crashed.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:15.860
Thousands of houses that were still in the
middle of development were simply never finished

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:20.400
and were abandoned due to a lack of funds
and falling demand.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:25.680
These abandoned residential estates were given
highly optimistic names such as "Paradise

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:29.550
Valley", however, today, they're nothing of
the sort.

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:34.599
They're extremely creepy to witness and are
reminiscent of a post-apocalyptic Desperate

00:04:34.599 --> 00:04:35.599
Housewives.

00:04:35.599 --> 00:04:37.660
Man that would be a good show!

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:42.129
They have since come to be known as the "Ghosts
Estates" of Ireland.

00:04:42.129 --> 00:04:45.569
Somewhere that looks this creepy just has
to be haunted.

00:04:45.569 --> 00:04:49.669
Seeing these makes you think how strange our
world would appear if all the humans suddenly

00:04:49.669 --> 00:04:51.129
disappeared.

00:04:51.129 --> 00:04:56.080
Just a splattering of human life makes all
the difference between a cosy, welcoming home

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:59.650
and this unnerving scene.

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:04.349
During World War II the British Navy built
an array of sea forts just off the southeast

00:05:04.349 --> 00:05:09.600
coast of England called the Maunsell Forts,
also commonly referred to as the Red Sands

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:10.600
Sea Forts.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:16.270
They may look like AT-AT Walkers but their
purpose was not to attack, but to defend the

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:19.909
United Kingdom, against German air raids.

00:05:19.909 --> 00:05:23.379
Following the war, they were decommissioned
in the 1950s.

00:05:23.379 --> 00:05:28.379
Shortly afterwards they were used as pirate
radio stations to broadcast illegal radio

00:05:28.379 --> 00:05:30.020
waves across the United Kingdom.

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:34.909
Until they were shut down by the British government
in 1967.

00:05:34.909 --> 00:05:39.749
Ever since, the forts have been abandoned
and now stand as an eerie reminder of a truly

00:05:39.749 --> 00:05:42.069
horrific part of history.

00:05:42.069 --> 00:05:47.600
There is however, a dispute going on over
who actually owns these forts.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:54.430
A man named Paddy Roy Bates purchased the
nearby Rough Sands Fort in 1964 and lived

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:55.499
in it.

00:05:55.499 --> 00:06:01.900
He decided to declare the fort as his own
country, named the "Principality of Sealand".

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:07.349
He then told all the other countries in Europe
that Sealand was an official principality...

00:06:07.349 --> 00:06:10.969
and they all said "no, no it's not".

00:06:10.969 --> 00:06:16.410
Bates however was adamant that Sealand should
be an officially recognised nation and to

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:22.249
prove his point he claimed the Maunsell Forts
as official land and property of Sealand.

00:06:22.249 --> 00:06:24.509
Yeah, that’ll show em!

00:06:24.509 --> 00:06:25.639
Erm, no.

00:06:25.639 --> 00:06:29.169
England basically said, "I don’t think so
old chap, they're ours!

00:06:29.169 --> 00:06:30.199
Give them back you freewheeling pirate".

00:06:30.199 --> 00:06:35.060
The debate over their ownership and whether
the Principality of Sealand even exists, still

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:37.509
goes on to this day.

00:06:37.509 --> 00:06:40.300
Just to clarify things, it totally doesn't
exist.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:46.050
The United Nations Convention on the Law of
the Sea states, "Artificial islands, installations

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:48.939
and structures do not possess the status of
islands.

00:06:48.939 --> 00:06:52.039
They have no territorial sea of their own."

00:06:52.039 --> 00:06:54.550
Yeah, sorry about that Sealand.

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:58.990
Next up is this UFO like structure called
Buzludzha.

00:06:58.990 --> 00:07:04.439
First opened in 1981, it was the home of the
Bulgarian Communist Party during the Soviet

00:07:04.439 --> 00:07:05.439
Era.

00:07:05.439 --> 00:07:08.569
Because a rectangular building is far too
capitalist.

00:07:08.569 --> 00:07:14.839
This impressive piece of soviet architecture
sits in the Central Balkan Mountains in Bulgaria.

00:07:14.839 --> 00:07:19.409
It was this ominous building where some of
the most infamous and controversial politics

00:07:19.409 --> 00:07:22.229
originated from during the Cold War.

00:07:22.229 --> 00:07:28.139
But when the Iron Curtain fell in 1990, marking
the end of the Soviet regime, the Buzludzha

00:07:28.139 --> 00:07:30.699
was completely abandoned.

00:07:30.699 --> 00:07:36.300
What was once a political powerhouse and a
global symbol of communism is now just a chilling

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:37.770
piece of history.

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:40.560
Left to succumb to the whims of the snow and
ice.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:45.089
The building is now completely in ruins and
stepping inside it feels like entering some

00:07:45.089 --> 00:07:49.050
kind of communist alien spacecraft, if that's
even a thing.

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:53.559
I wonder if they do have communism in space.

00:07:53.559 --> 00:07:58.910
The Ryugyong Hotel in North Korea's capital,
Pyongyang, is not as totally abandoned as

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:03.409
the other locations on this list, but that
doesn't change the fact that it's bloody creepy!

00:08:03.409 --> 00:08:08.719
Construction of this monolithic ode to failed
communism began in 1987.

00:08:08.719 --> 00:08:13.740
When North Korea was looking somewhat prosperous
and was expecting an influx of tourists to

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:17.219
witness the self-styled "greatest nation on
Earth".

00:08:17.219 --> 00:08:20.219
"Build it and they will come" someone told
Kim Il-sung.

00:08:20.219 --> 00:08:23.340
But in the end, no one came.

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:29.959
The Soviet Union fell and in 1992 North Korea
ceased construction due to lack of funds.

00:08:29.959 --> 00:08:33.340
You’ve got to give it to them; they don’t
do things by halves.

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:37.789
If North Korea wants to build a tourist hotel,
they’re gonna build a bloody big one.

00:08:37.789 --> 00:08:42.509
This 105-floor giant has stood completely
empty ever since.

00:08:42.509 --> 00:08:48.089
It's now, no more than an overwhelming monument
to the utopia that North Korea has tried ever

00:08:48.089 --> 00:08:55.100
so hard to achieve, but for the poor, unfortunate
residents of the country, has sadly, failed.

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:59.810
Things started to appear hopeful in 2008,
when North Korea announced that they had resumed

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:01.630
work on the hotel.

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:06.269
Then in 2011 the exterior was eventually completed
with glass panels.

00:09:06.269 --> 00:09:09.720
It now looks slightly less intimidating.

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:14.860
Although the excitement was short lived, North
Korea couldn't muster up enough funds to complete

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:15.860
the interior.

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:16.860
So all they actually achieved was polishing
their monumental, empty turd.

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:21.430
The opening of the hotel has been scheduled
numerous times in recent years, but every

00:09:21.430 --> 00:09:23.279
time, it has been postponed.

00:09:23.279 --> 00:09:27.910
Probably due to the fact that if you step
inside the hotel it's still a completely empty

00:09:27.910 --> 00:09:28.910
shell.

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:31.470
At least that's what some sources say.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:34.529
After all North Korea is an extremely secretive
place.

00:09:34.529 --> 00:09:38.560
Who knows what's actually going on inside
there, they could be building North Korea's

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:40.670
very own Disneyland for all we know.

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:44.470
Or more likely, concealing a missile factory.

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:49.790
In the Zhejiang province of Eastern China
sits a large lake that holds an underwater

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:50.790
secret.

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:55.389
The lake is called Qiandao Lake, which translates
as "Thousand Island Lake".

00:09:55.389 --> 00:10:01.850
At the bottom of this enormous body of water
sits a forgotten ancient city called Shi Cheng,

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:04.190
which means "Lion City".

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:08.860
The underwater city of Shi Cheng is basically
like the lost city of Atlantis, except we

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:10.680
know where this one is.

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:13.420
Also Shi Cheng was never actually lost in
the first place.

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:15.730
It was simply flooded and abandoned.

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:20.890
At one time Shi Cheng was the centre of economics
and politics in Eastern China.

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:26.149
It was a huge, beautiful city, full of dazzling
white temples and arches, paved roads and

00:10:26.149 --> 00:10:27.660
thousands of houses.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:33.360
The city is steeped in heritage and culture;
built 1,300 years ago, this large, ancient

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:38.100
city covered an area of approximately 62 football
fields.

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:43.680
But the Chinese Government was obviously more
concerned with energy revenues than preserving

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:45.269
cultural heritage.

00:10:45.269 --> 00:10:51.790
Because in 1959, the Chinese government flooded
the valley that Shi Cheng sits in, to make

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:53.560
a new, artificial lake.

00:10:53.560 --> 00:10:55.350
For what purpose?

00:10:55.350 --> 00:11:00.310
Well they decided a new hydroelectric power
station was required and this would be the

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:01.310
ideal location.

00:11:01.310 --> 00:11:02.310
Makes sense; a country with nearly a million
square kilometres of land, which is mostly

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:03.310
uninhabited and they decided to flood a city
with incredible cultural significance to make

00:11:03.310 --> 00:11:04.310
room for it.

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:07.819
This gigantic man-made reservoir, which has
been named Qiandao Lake, now hides, what was

00:11:07.819 --> 00:11:13.620
once, and in some respects still is, one of
the most beautiful cities that China has ever

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:14.620
known.

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:19.259
And lastly we have the radioactive city of
Pripyat.

00:11:19.259 --> 00:11:24.350
On the 26th April 1986 at reactor four of
the Chernobyl Nuclear Power Plant in Ukraine,

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:28.690
an argument broke out between two senior nuclear
engineers.

00:11:28.690 --> 00:11:33.860
Over whether or not they should run a potentially
dangerous test on the reactor.

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:39.980
They ended up running the test and the nuclear
reactor core malfunctioned and tragically

00:11:39.980 --> 00:11:41.040
exploded.

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:46.629
Over the following weeks many tonnes of highly
radioactive Caesium-137 was leaked into the

00:11:46.629 --> 00:11:49.589
atmosphere from the still-burning reactor
core.

00:11:49.589 --> 00:11:52.829
The nuclear fallout from the disaster covered
much of Europe.

00:11:52.829 --> 00:11:57.889
One of the worst affected areas was the nearby
city of Pripyat, which was built to house

00:11:57.889 --> 00:12:00.939
workers at the Chernobyl Nuclear Power Plant.

00:12:00.939 --> 00:12:08.300
In total 350,400 people from Pripyat and from
other towns several miles around the disaster

00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:12.209
area, were permanently evacuated from their
homes.

00:12:12.209 --> 00:12:17.750
An area covering 1,000 square miles around
the Chernobyl Plant was completely abandoned

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:22.480
due to it being contaminated with fatal levels
of radiation.

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:29.439
This area, known as the "exclusion zone" or
"zone of alienation", is now the most severely

00:12:29.439 --> 00:12:31.980
abandoned place on Earth.

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:36.980
Nature has taken over, and animals, heavily
disfigured by radiation, run wild.

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:42.500
With no human competition, these mutant animals
have claimed the exclusion zone as their own.

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:45.910
It's like an alien landscape crossed with
post-apocalyptic desolation.

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:50.620
If it weren’t so radioactive it would be
the perfect spot for a game of paintball.

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:57.079
The trees in a 4 square mile area, surrounding
the reactor core, received a severely large

00:12:57.079 --> 00:13:00.370
dose of radiation and were subsequently killed.

00:13:00.370 --> 00:13:04.199
The radiation caused them to turn an eerie
reddish-brown colour.

00:13:04.199 --> 00:13:08.170
Because of this the area has been given the
name of the "Red Forest".

00:13:08.170 --> 00:13:12.670
The Red Forest is one of the most radioactive
places in the world today.

00:13:12.670 --> 00:13:16.740
Scientists say the exclusion zone will not
be safe enough for humans to re-inhabit for

00:13:16.740 --> 00:13:18.319
another 20,000 years.

00:13:18.319 --> 00:13:25.220
Until then it serves as a huge, living laboratory
for scientists to measure the effects of radiation

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:27.910
poisoning on animals and wildlife.

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:36.119
As well as a memorial to the worst nuclear
tragedy that has ever happened.

